From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:02:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Walk the row groups to write by index, so the assert-only binding goes

RowGroup::WriteToDisk() binds each row group of the batch to a name
that only D_ASSERT() reads, so in a release build, where D_ASSERT()
expands to nothing, every iteration holds an unused variable and
-Wunused-variable says so. The loop walks the batch by index and the
assertion indexes it, which is the shape upstream gives the loop
later; nothing else in the loop read the binding.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group.cpp
index e440140659..8a3b0beed1 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group.cpp
@@ -1044,8 +1044,8 @@ vector<RowGroupWriteData> RowGroup::WriteToDisk(RowGroupWriteInfo &info,
 	}
 
 	idx_t column_count = row_groups[0].get().GetColumnCount();
-	for (auto &row_group : row_groups) {
-		D_ASSERT(column_count == row_group.get().GetColumnCount());
+	for (idx_t row_group_idx = 0; row_group_idx < row_groups.size(); row_group_idx++) {
+		D_ASSERT(column_count == row_groups[row_group_idx].get().GetColumnCount());
 		RowGroupWriteData write_data;
 		write_data.states.reserve(column_count);
 		write_data.statistics.reserve(column_count);
